# Analytics Service Environment Variables
# Copy this file to .env and update with your actual values

## Core Infrastructure
NODE_ENV=development
PORT=3005

## Database
# Least-privilege application role (NOSUPERUSER, NOBYPASSRLS, non-owner) so RLS enforces.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://telemetry_app:telemetry_app_local_dev@localhost:5432/telemetry

## Cache
REDIS_URL=redis://localhost:6379

## Observability
OTEL_EXPORTER_OTLP_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:4318
LOG_LEVEL=debug

## Service-to-service auth
# Shared with the gateway, which attaches it to every proxied /v1/analytics request. Required,
# no default: analytics-service does not start without it, and it must be at least 32 characters
# after trimming and contain only printable ASCII.
#
# This line is an addition, not a value change: before S-9 this file declared no
# INTERNAL_API_SECRET at all (`git show HEAD:apps/analytics-service/.env.example` has no such
# line). The value matches apps/gateway/.env.example -- the service that *sends* the header --
# and also the repo-root .env.example and apps/usage-service/.env.example. It deliberately does
# NOT match billing's and worker's, which carry a different string; do not "correct" it to
# theirs.
#
# Re-derived at S-9's Gate-4 Round 2: SIX .env.example files declare this variable (the repo root
# included, which an earlier version of this comment missed) and they carry TWO distinct values --
# four of this one, two of billing's and worker's. Pre-existing, live, and recorded as S-58 in
# .claude/rules/known-gaps.md. Measured through billing's real guard factory: a gateway holding
# this value is answered 401 by a service holding billing's.
#
# docker/docker-compose.yml is a separate, self-consistent world: all five service blocks carry
# ci-internal-api-secret-with-at-least-32-chars, which is why this file does not.
INTERNAL_API_SECRET=dev-local-internal-secret-at-least-32-chars
